(216, 199, 'text', '<div style=\"background:#f0f4ff;border:1px solid #c7d7ff;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;color:#3b5bdb;margin-bottom:8px;\">🖼️ Suggested Images — Ek choose karke topic image set karo:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-bottom:10px;\">Search: unsupervised learning clustering dimensionality reduction density estimation</p>\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;\">\r\n<a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&q=unsupervised+learning+clustering+dimensionality+reduction+density+estimation\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#4285f4;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🔍 Google Images</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://unsplash.com/s/photos/unsupervised+learning+clustering+dimensionality+reduction+density+estimation\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#111;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🌄 Unsplash</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/search/unsupervised+learning+clustering+dimensionality+reduction+density+estimation/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#05a081;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">📸 Pexels</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://pixabay.com/images/search/unsupervised+learning+clustering+dimensionality+reduction+density+estimation/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#2ec66e;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🎨 Pixabay</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://www.freepik.com/search?query=unsupervised+learning+clustering+dimensionality+reduction+density+estimation\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background:#ff5a5a;color:#fff;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:6px;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;\">🖌️ Freepik</a>\r\n</div></div><h3>Introduction to Unsupervised Learning</h3><p>Unsupervised learning is a type of machine learning where the model is trained on unlabeled data, and it tries to find patterns, relationships, or structure in the data. In this section, we will cover three important topics in unsupervised learning: clustering, dimensionality reduction, and density estimation.</p><h3>Clustering</h3><p>Clustering is a technique used to group similar data points into clusters. The goal of clustering is to identify patterns or structures in the data that are not easily visible by other methods. There are many clustering algorithms, including K-Means, Hierarchical Clustering, and DBSCAN.</p><p>Let\'s consider an example of K-Means clustering using Python and the Scikit-learn library:</p><pre><code>from sklearn.cluster import KMeans\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Generate some random data\nnp.random.seed(0)\ndata = np.random.rand(100, 2)\n\n# Create a KMeans model with 3 clusters\nkmeans = KMeans(n_clusters=3)\n\n# Fit the model to the data\nkmeans.fit(data)\n\n# Predict the cluster labels\nlabels = kmeans.predict(data)\n\n# Print the cluster labels\nprint(labels)</code></pre><h3>Dimensionality Reduction</h3><p>Dimensionality reduction is a technique used to reduce the number of features or dimensions in a dataset. This can be useful for visualizing high-dimensional data, reducing noise, or improving the performance of machine learning models. There are many dimensionality reduction algorithms, including Principal Component Analysis (PCA), t-SNE, and Autoencoders.</p><p>Let\'s consider an example of PCA using Python and the Scikit-learn library:</p><pre><code>from sklearn.decomposition import PCA\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Generate some random data\nnp.random.seed(0)\ndata = np.random.rand(100, 10)\n\n# Create a PCA model with 2 components\npca = PCA(n_components=2)\n\n# Fit the model to the data\npca.fit(data)\n\n# Transform the data\ntransformed_data = pca.transform(data)\n\n# Print the transformed data\nprint(transformed_data)</code></pre><h3>Density Estimation</h3><p>Density estimation is a technique used to estimate the underlying probability distribution of a dataset. This can be useful for identifying outliers, visualizing the distribution of the data, or generating new data samples. There are many density estimation algorithms, including Histograms, Kernel Density Estimation (KDE), and Gaussian Mixture Models (GMMs).</p><p>Let\'s consider an example of KDE using Python and the Scikit-learn library:</p><pre><code>from sklearn.neighbors import KernelDensity\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Generate some random data\nnp.random.seed(0)\ndata = np.random.rand(100, 1)\n\n# Create a KDE model with a Gaussian kernel\nkde = KernelDensity(kernel=\'gaussian\', bandwidth=0.5)\n\n# Fit the model to the data\nkde.fit(data)\n\n# Evaluate the model on a grid of points\ngrid = np.linspace(0, 1, 100).reshape(-1, 1)\ndensity = kde.score_samples(grid)\n\n# Print the density values\nprint(density)</code></pre><p>In conclusion, unsupervised learning is a powerful tool for discovering patterns and structure in data. Clustering, dimensionality reduction, and density estimation are all important techniques in unsupervised learning, and can be used in a variety of applications, including data visualization, anomaly detection, and recommender systems.</p><ul><li><strong>Key Takeaways:</strong></li><li>Clustering is used to group similar data points into clusters.</li><li>Dimensionality reduction is used to reduce the number of features or dimensions in a dataset.</li><li>Density estimation is used to estimate the underlying probability distribution of a dataset.</li></ul>', 1, '2026-04-04 02:05:54', '2026-04-04 02:05:54');
